/INPUT CAN BE DISABLED BY GROUNDING
/LEVEL 0 SENSE LINE.
/MISSED EVENTS ARE SIGNALED BY "EVENT"
/AN OVERFLOWING SUM IS BY "OVERFLOW"
/DISABLED CONDITION IS ALSO SIGNALLED.
/
/INPUT EVENT ON CLOCK CHANNEL TWO.
/
/RSW 0-5 CONTROL VIEWED CHANNELS
/SNS 0-5 MOVE TRACES TO RIGHT
/A/D 0-5 CONTROL VERTICAL FOR TRACES
/DATA IS ACCUMULATED IN FIELDS 0-5
/DATA IS IN THREE EPOCHS WORDS 2000-
/3377
/WORDS 3400-3777 ARE USED FOR AVERAGING
/RSW 6 DISPLAYS INTEGRAL, STIM NUMBER &
/      TOTAL COUNTS FOR EACH CHANNEL.
/RSW 7 MOVES INTEGRAL LINE TO RIGHT
/HIT 0-5 ON TTY TO CHANGE CHANNELS.
/LSW BITS 8-11 MAGNIFY INTEGRAL.
/A/D 6 CONTROLS VERTICAL FOR INTEGRAL
/RSW 8 ON ABORTS TAPEWRITE.
/RSW 9-11 CONTROLS DISPLAY TIME
/RSW 9-11 = 0 ZERO DISPLAY TIME
/RSW 9-11 = 7 INFINATE DISPLAY
/APPLY EVENT TO CLOCK CHANNEL TWO.
/DATA IS STORED STARTING WITH SELECTED
/BLOCK, IN GROUPS OF SIX BLOCKS.
/PROGRAM HALTS AT BLOCK 777.
/
/PROGRAMMER
/DAN GRAY
/10/10/72
